---
/**
 * Terms of service. Draft, for the same reason as the privacy policy: the app's
 * own terms text, with the entity, jurisdiction and fee questions still open
 * (landing/STATUS.md).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import DocLayout from '../components/DocLayout.astro'
import { BRAND } from '../config/site'
import { breadcrumbLd } from '../lib/ld'
---

<Base path="/terms" extraLd={[breadcrumbLd([{ name: 'Terms', path: '/terms' }])]}>
  <DocLayout path="/terms" title="Terms of service" lead="The terms for using an OR² workspace, in plain language." meta={`Effective date to be confirmed · ${BRAND.legalName}`}>
    <div class="notice" slot="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Draft — needs owner and legal review before it is relied on.</strong> The clauses
        below follow the structure {BRAND.name} already publishes. The registered entity, its
        address, the fee and cancellation terms, and the dispute forum are still to be confirmed
        by {BRAND.legalName} and by a lawyer.
      </p>
    </div>


    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These terms govern the use of {BRAND.name}, the business-operations platform operated by{' '}
      {BRAND.legalName}. By using the service, your business agrees to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided to registered businesses. Your workspace administrator provisions
      accounts for the people in your business who need access.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Accounts are provisioned by your administrator, not by individual sign-up.</li>
      <li>Keep your credentials confidential.</li>
      <li>Activity carried out under your account is treated as your business's activity.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. The service</h2>
    <p>
      {BRAND.name} is a business-operations platform. It lets a business track stock, record
      purchases and sales, manage payments, keep ledgers, monitor cash flow and produce reports,
      all within a single workspace that is isolated to that business.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Use the service for lawful business purposes only.</li>
      <li>Do not interfere with, overload or attempt to disrupt the service.</li>
      <li>Do not attempt to access another business's workspace or data.</li>
      <li>Do not misuse data that belongs to another business or another person.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Your data and ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Your business owns its records. Everything you and your team enter, from products and bills
      to payments, ledgers and reports, belongs to your business.
    </p>
    <p>
      {BRAND.legalName} owns the platform: the service, its software and its trademarks. These
      terms grant your business the right to use the service; they do not transfer any ownership of
      the platform to you.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Service availability</h2>
    <p>
      We operate the service on a best-effort basis and work to keep it continuously available. The
      counter is designed to keep billing offline; offline bills stay provisional until confirmed, and
      you should test this on your own devices and network.
      Planned maintenance is scheduled to avoid disrupting trading hours wherever possible.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service is not offered with a specific uptime guarantee, and we do not claim one. No
      availability figure is published on this site.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Fees and access</h2>
    <p>
      Plan prices are listed on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a> (Basic and Pro monthly, with a
      7-day free trial; Custom priced with you). No payment is taken on this website yet; how
      payment is collected will be added to these terms before billing starts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The billing period, the payment terms, any advance paid and the treatment of an advance on
      cancellation are terms of your service agreement. They are to be set out by {BRAND.legalName}
      before these terms take effect, and are summarised at{' '}
      <a href="/refund-cancellation">cancellations and refunds</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Confidentiality and security</h2>
    <p>
      Each workspace is isolated to its business, and business records are never visible to, or
      shared with, another business. We protect data with encryption in transit, controlled access
      and least-privilege administration.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for the accuracy of the
      records entered in your workspace.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, the service is provided "as is" and "as available", without
      warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including any implied warranties of
      merchantability or fitness for a particular purpose.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, {BRAND.legalName} will not be liable for indirect,
      incidental, special or consequential losses, or for loss of profits or data arising from use
      of the service. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      Your workspace administrator may manage, suspend or remove user accounts within your
      business's workspace.
    </p>
    <p>
      When a business's use of the service ends, its business data is returned or deleted at the
      administrator's instruction. Deletion is complete, with no history and no footprints.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      If we change these terms, we will give reasonable advance notice through the service before
      the changes take effect. Continued use of the service after changes take effect constitutes
      acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of India. The exclusive forum for disputes, and the
      place of arbitration if any, are to be confirmed by {BRAND.legalName} before these terms
      take effect.
    </p>

    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms are handled through your workspace administrator.</p>

    <h2>15. Schedule to be completed by {BRAND.legalName}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Registered entity name, registered address and jurisdiction.</li>
      <li>Governing law forum and any dispute resolution mechanism.</li>
      <li>Fee, billing period, payment terms and the treatment of an advance.</li>
      <li>Notice period for ending an access arrangement.</li>
      <li>Effective date.</li>
    </ul>

  </DocLayout>
</Base>
